--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

reference/archetypes.toml
  The figure archetype taxonomy (five domains, 17 chart types) and the per-type
  mandatory-element lists are adapted from:
    quaresma00/medical-sci-figure-skill  (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 quaresma00)
    https://github.com/quaresma00/medical-sci-figure-skill
  Element lists were reduced to what is mechanically verifiable; the detectors in
  tools/figures/elements.py are original. Text was rephrased.

tools/figures/elements.py
  glyph_warnings() and tick_label_collisions() are adapted from the QA engine of
  quaresma00/medical-sci-figure-skill (MIT), which credits scipilot-figure-skill
  for the originals. Reimplemented to emit structured results for the gate rather
  than printing.

tools/figures/style.py
  Journal palette values (NEJM, Lancet, JAMA, JCO, Nature) as published in ggsci
  (Nan Xiao; ggsci is GPL-3, the colour values themselves are the journals' own
  brand colours and are used here as data, not as code).
  Sizing and rcParams conventions informed by SciencePlots, tueplots and
  publication-plot-settings; no code was copied.

reference/figure-standards.md
  Publisher requirements summarised, with links, from Wiley Author Services,
  Springer submission guidelines, IEEE graphics guidelines, ASPET digital art
  guidelines, Nature artwork guidance and Canadian Science Publishing. Content
  was rephrased; verify the binding requirements against your target journal.
